From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:04:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: gs201: add the GSA mailbox

Add the GSA mailbox node at 0x17c90000 with its response interrupt (GIC
SPI 363), as in the stock device tree. Leave it disabled: nothing uses
it until the AoC bring-up enables it.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201.dtsi | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201.dtsi
index a9b4470bd..8f06a7666 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201.dtsi
@@ -1409,6 +1409,12 @@ ufs_0_phy: phy@14704000 {
 			status = "disabled";
 		};
 
+		gsa: gsa@17c90000 {
+			compatible = "google,gs201-gsa";
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 363 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
 		/*
 		 * Multi-core timer. Gives the kernel a broadcast clock event
 		 * device that keeps running while cores are powered down in C2.
